	quest.0A34FD02D54EA6A2.quest_desc: ["Crafting Monitor is a network access and operator interface in an AE2 system. The item is useful only when its power, channel, storage and routing assumptions are explicit and the network remains diagnosable under load.","Acceptance: verify access scope, crafting visibility, permission boundary, search behaviour and disconnected-state clarity; run a representative automated job, record channel and power use, test a full or disconnected destination, and prove that loot, rewards, trades or alternate recipes cannot unlock this capability before its stage."]
	quest.0A34FD02D54EA6A2.title: "Crafting Monitor — Network Acceptance"
	quest.0A5C03A114ABF62D.quest_desc: ["Maxwell is a cross-mod endgame prerequisite consumed by Fragmentum convergence in the Heart of the Void convergence. Its narrative significance must be backed by an authoritative, irreversible production route and a bounded operational role—not by experience, duplicate materials or a lore-book reward that substitutes for actual endgame proof.","Acceptance: verify its source mod progression, assigned stage, exact count, irreversible consumption, blacklist and bypass coverage and proof that Fragmentum does not fabricate or refund it; trace every major prerequisite branch, reconcile the consumed assemblies, perform one representative bounded capability test, document an interruption or loss-recovery procedure and confirm that quest rewards, EMC, simulation, trade, loot rerolls, recursive crafting and duplication cannot create the artifact or its protected inputs."]
	quest.0A5C03A114ABF62D.quest_subtitle: "A reward wouldn't be useful enough for those who have made it this far..."
	quest.0A7940B06E7A3A56.quest_desc: ["Dank Storages is a cross-mod survival or workshop support component in the survival-foundations route. It should establish a safe, repeatable capability and prepare the next production step—not act as a reason to distribute ordinary materials or XP from the quest book.","Acceptance: verify which current-stage need it solves, its material ancestry, repair or refill route, limitations and why it does not grant a later technology or resource early; demonstrate a representative use, record the input, durability or reserve and output, test one loss or blocked state, keep an ordinary replacement route and remove item, XP, loot and random-reward shortcuts."]
	quest.0A7940B06E7A3A56.title: "Dank Storages — Foundation Acceptance"
	quest.0A912B2E2BE34920.quest_desc: ["Gas Lift / Drill Pipe / Seismic Sensor is a specialized PneumaticCraft component in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify its pressure, heat, air, program or logistics contract and a safe blocked, empty or overpressure state; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.0AA074D4F7CBCED1.quest_desc: ["Gem Cutting Table is a gem, socketing or gem-processing component in the Apotheosis progression system. It must be treated as a controlled upgrade or encounter tool whose value comes from measured build improvement, recoverable materials and explicit risk—not from a quest reward that skips the affix economy.","Acceptance: verify gem tier and trait, socket count, insertion and removal route, dust yield, compatibility with the target item and protection against destroying an irreplaceable build; record the before-and-after equipment state, resource cost and failure condition, test one representative combat or enchanting cycle, salvage or recover rejected results and confirm that rewards, rerolls, duplication and unrestricted boss spawning cannot bypass the intended progression."]
	quest.0AA72D6706542CA6.quest_desc: ["Charger is a crystal and network-material production step in an AE2 system. The item is useful only when its power, channel, storage and routing assumptions are explicit and the network remains diagnosable under load.","Acceptance: verify crystal source, charging or growth time, batch buffer and contamination-free conversion; run a representative automated job, record channel and power use, test a full or disconnected destination, and prove that loot, rewards, trades or alternate recipes cannot unlock this capability before its stage."]
	quest.0AA72D6706542CA6.title: "Charger — Network Acceptance"
	quest.0ABDED0707E01F06.quest_desc: [
		"The Sack of Sating must be fed by right-clicking edible items into it, similar to storing items in a Bundle. When fed, it irreversibly stores the hunger value of the items within itself. If fed food contained in Bowls or Bottles, the Sack of Sating will return the Bowl or Bottle."
		""
		"When the player becomes hungry, the Sack of Sating will passively feed them, replenishing 1 (🍗) hunger every 5 seconds (100 ticks). This effect will stack if the player has multiple Sack of Sating in their inventory."
		""
		"&4Feeding the Sack of Sating certain items (like the Eternal Steak from the Artifacts mod) will cause it and the item to explode, creating an effect similar to a Nuclear Bomb, but pink and smaller. Be warned that this explosion may harm or kill the player."
	]
	quest.0ABDED0707E01F06.quest_subtitle: "Freaky ahh sack"
	quest.0AC7D844C55119E1.quest_desc: ["Wrench is a specialized Modern Industrialization component in Modern Industrialization. The real requirement is a stable material and machine network with controlled voltage, fluids, byproducts and throughput rather than possession of one block.","Acceptance: verify its material, voltage, fluid, tool, machine or multiblock contract and a safe blocked or unpowered state; complete a representative unattended batch, record energy, fluid and material reserves, test full output or power loss, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.0ACCCC1B217D98D0.quest_desc: ["Quantum Structure is a cross-mod AE2 integration component in an AE2 system. The item is useful only when its power, channel, storage and routing assumptions are explicit and the network remains diagnosable under load.","Acceptance: verify the external mod's stage, conversion direction, component data and the absence of a cheaper parallel route; run a representative automated job, record channel and power use, test a full or disconnected destination, and prove that loot, rewards, trades or alternate recipes cannot unlock this capability before its stage."]
	quest.0AD6897A8AB1CC5D.quest_desc: ["Oil Hammer is a specialized TFMG metallurgy component in the TFMG metallurgy route. The lesson must establish repeatable coke, refractory, iron or steel production with measured yield and recoverable multiblocks—not reward the player with the same fuel or metal being requested.","Acceptance: verify its material ancestry, heat and fuel contract, multiblock or fabrication role, measured yield, byproduct route, safe cooldown and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; run a representative heat or casting batch, record fuel, ore, flux, temperature or cycle time, metal and byproducts, test blocked output or fuel loss, cool and recover safely, and remove item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.0ADA2391DDE7466E.quest_desc: ["Engine Controller is a electromechanical generation or conversion machine in the TFMG electrical route. The lesson must establish a measured and protected power capability with reproducible conductor and component supply—not reward the player with the same wire, magnet or capacitor being requested.","Acceptance: verify mechanical input or electrical output, rotational speed, sustained generation, load response, startup reserve, idle loss and controlled shutdown under overload; build or operate a representative circuit, record voltage, current or capacity and the limiting component, test overload, empty generation or disconnected output, recover safely and remove material, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.0ADEFF34AAA0D7C7.quest_subtitle: "Used to make a Printed Dimensional Processor"
	quest.0AE0E5AA8FB69FE2.quest_subtitle: "Gadgets for all situations"
	quest.0AE0E5AA8FB69FE2.title: "Welcome to Create:Connected"
	quest.0AE4B0BD9B765D60.quest_desc: ["Surface Scanner / Machine Input is a specialized TFMG metallurgy component in the TFMG metallurgy route. The lesson must establish repeatable coke, refractory, iron or steel production with measured yield and recoverable multiblocks—not reward the player with the same fuel or metal being requested.","Acceptance: verify its material ancestry, heat and fuel contract, multiblock or fabrication role, measured yield, byproduct route, safe cooldown and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; run a representative heat or casting batch, record fuel, ore, flux, temperature or cycle time, metal and byproducts, test blocked output or fuel loss, cool and recover safely, and remove item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.0AEAEA976ED0C470.quest_desc: ["Charging Station is a specialized PneumaticCraft component in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify its pressure, heat, air, program or logistics contract and a safe blocked, empty or overpressure state; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.0AEDFC064B84C877.quest_desc: [
		"Autocrafting is one of the primary functions of AE2. Instead of manually having to craft the correct number of each sub-ingredient and labor away like some sort of plebian, you can ask your ME system to do it for you. Or automatically craft items and export them somewhere. Or automatically keep certain amounts of items in stock through clever emergent behavior. It also works with fluids, and, if you have certain addons for extra mod material types, like Mekanism gasses, those materials too. It's pretty great."
		""
		"It is quite a complex topic, so strap in and let's go."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"An autocrafting setup consists of 3 things:"
		""
		"The thing sending the crafting request"
		"The crafting CPU"
		"The ME Pattern Provider."
		"Here is what happens:"
		""
		"Something creates a crafting request. This can be you in the terminal clicking on something autocraftable, or an export bus or interface with a crafting card requesting one of the item they're set to export/stock."
		"(IMPORTANT: use whatever you have bound to \"pick block\" (usually middle-mouse) to request crafts of something you already have in stock, this can conflict with inventory sorting mods),"
		"The ME system calculates the required ingredients and prerequisite crafting steps to fulfill the request, and stores them in the selected crafting CPU"
		""
		"The ME Pattern Provider with the relevant pattern pushes the ingredients specified in the pattern to any adjacent inventory. In the case of a crafting table recipe (a \"crafting pattern\") this will be a Molecular Assembler. In the case of a non-crafting recipe (a \"processing pattern\") this will be some other block or machine or elaborate redstone-controlled setup."
		""
		"The result of the craft is returned to the system somehow, be it by import bus, interface, or pushing the result back into a pattern provider. Note that an \"item entering system\" event must occur, you can't just pipe the result into a chest with a ME Storage Bus on it."
		""
		"If that craft is a prerequisite for another craft in the request, the items are stored in that crafting CPU and then used in that craft."
	]
	quest.0AEDFC064B84C877.title: "Auto-Crafting"
	quest.0AFFE685B5B34A56.quest_desc: ["Packaging Provider is a specialized packaged-automation component in the Packaged Automation branch. It must execute an explicit recipe contract with complete inputs, a single accountable output and deterministic recovery—not act as a shortcut whose quest reward supplies black iron, awakened material or cosmic components.","Acceptance: verify contract inputs, package identity, supported recipe tier, energy or fluid cost, atomic output, backpressure, restart recovery and absence of duplicate retained contents; encode one representative recipe, submit exactly one bounded input set, reconcile package contents and final output, test missing-input, full-output and restart states, recover every retained item and confirm that rewards, duplicate packages, recursive unpacking and parallel endpoint races cannot create extra material."]
	quest.0AFFE685B5B34A56.title: "Packaging Provider — Atomic Automation Acceptance"
	quest.0B009391E3F76D6E.quest_desc: ["Settlement Management Checkpoint 6D6E is a settlement systems-design checkpoint in the MineColonies settlement route. The lesson is a staffed, supplied and recoverable civic service with measurable demand and output—not a reward for placing one hut or triggering an advancement.","Acceptance: verify population and staffing map, food and tool reserves, warehouse and courier capacity, production bottlenecks, defence coverage, research priority and recovery after losing one essential service; staff and supply the service, run a representative work cycle, record requests, delivery delay and output, test worker absence or blocked storage, recover without commands and remove material, XP, loot and advancement-reward incentives."]
	quest.0B1DF8A040826D87.quest_desc: ["Insanite Ingot is a reactor fuel or structural feedstock in the Extreme Reactors power branch. It must be accepted as part of a complete, instrumented multiblock whose fuel, heat, waste, coolant and output are reconciled—not as an isolated block or reward-funded power shortcut.","Acceptance: verify legal ore source, processing yield, fuel composition, batch mass, storage limit, consumption rate and prohibition on quest rewards or recycling creating more fresh fuel than was consumed; build or inspect the complete structure, record a cold baseline, run a bounded fuel batch, measure output and waste, test control-rod or emergency shutdown response, recover after full output or restart and confirm that rewards, duplicated fuel, free coolant and waste loops cannot create net power or gated materials."]
	quest.0B281C34E455EE72.quest_desc: ["Large Pumpjack Hammer Part / Large Pumpjack Hammer Head / Large Pumpjack Hammer Connector / Super Glue is a specialized TFMG metallurgy component in the TFMG metallurgy route. The lesson must establish repeatable coke, refractory, iron or steel production with measured yield and recoverable multiblocks—not reward the player with the same fuel or metal being requested.","Acceptance: verify its material ancestry, heat and fuel contract, multiblock or fabrication role, measured yield, byproduct route, safe cooldown and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; run a representative heat or casting batch, record fuel, ore, flux, temperature or cycle time, metal and byproducts, test blocked output or fuel loss, cool and recover safely, and remove item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.0B2DF0B5F4247A3F.quest_desc: ["Fluid Pipe / Steel Scaffolding Standard / Light Engineering / Rs Engineering is a industrial logistics, fluid or bulk-storage component in the Immersive Engineering route. The objective is a measurable, serviceable industrial capability with legal inputs and recoverable failure—not a random reward for crafting one block or tool.","Acceptance: verify medium ownership, direction, redstone state, filters and priorities, throughput, finite capacity, overflow route, loop prevention and recovery after one blocked segment; build or operate a representative installation, record input, output, power or fuel and limiting section, test blocked output or loss of supply, recover safely and remove random-table, item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.0B2DF0B5F4247A3F.title: "Fluid Pipe / Steel Scaffolding Standard / Light Engineering / Rs Engineering — Industrial Acceptance"
	quest.0B2FF8169FD3812D.quest_desc: ["Steel Item Output Hatch / Steel Item Input Hatch / Steel Fluid Input Hatch is a specialized Modern Industrialization component in Modern Industrialization. The real requirement is a stable material and machine network with controlled voltage, fluids, byproducts and throughput rather than possession of one block.","Acceptance: verify its material, voltage, fluid, tool, machine or multiblock contract and a safe blocked or unpowered state; complete a representative unattended batch, record energy, fluid and material reserves, test full output or power loss, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
