	quest.0EEA8C33BC327CCA.quest_desc: ["The Pattern Access Terminal serves to solve a specific issue: in a dense tower of ME Pattern Providers and Molecular Assemblers, you can't physically access the providers to insert new patterns. Additionally, perhaps you're lazy and don't want to walk across your base to insert a pattern. The pattern access terminal allows access to all pattern providers on the network."]
	quest.0EF4982211D87606.quest_desc: ["Morgan is a cross-mod endgame prerequisite consumed by Fragmentum convergence in the Heart of the Void convergence. Its narrative significance must be backed by an authoritative, irreversible production route and a bounded operational role—not by experience, duplicate materials or a lore-book reward that substitutes for actual endgame proof.","Acceptance: verify its source mod progression, assigned stage, exact count, irreversible consumption, blacklist and bypass coverage and proof that Fragmentum does not fabricate or refund it; trace every major prerequisite branch, reconcile the consumed assemblies, perform one representative bounded capability test, document an interruption or loss-recovery procedure and confirm that quest rewards, EMC, simulation, trade, loot rerolls, recursive crafting and duplication cannot create the artifact or its protected inputs."]
