	quest.22E01FE041DE9C54.quest_desc: ["Hydraulic Engine is a mechanical power source or engine module in the Create Stuff & Additions branch. It must be evaluated as part of a powered mechanical system with explicit fuel, stress, range or durability limits—not as a collectible item whose quest reward refunds its cost.","Acceptance: verify energy or fluid source, startup condition, stress capacity, sustained output, shutdown interlock, heat or pressure risk and comparison with the previous stage power source; document inputs and idle state, run one representative work cycle, measure consumption or operating duration, test blocked-output or low-power behavior, recover after interruption and confirm that quest rewards, duplicated fuel and free replacement parts cannot bypass the intended cost."]
	quest.22E15D3CC2162F60.quest_desc: ["Environmental Controller is a area-effect environmental system in the RFTools ecosystem. Its capability depends on modules, cards, power, area ownership and network configuration rather than on the block alone.","Acceptance: verify radius, module cost, energy demand, player or mob targeting, overlapping fields and server-side permission; run a representative automated cycle, record power and storage demand, test invalid configuration or a full destination, and close reward, loot, trade, quarry, duplication and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.22F4C38E79DEFF1E.quest_desc: ["Settlement Management Checkpoint FF1E is a settlement systems-design checkpoint in the MineColonies settlement route. The lesson is a staffed, supplied and recoverable civic service with measurable demand and output—not a reward for placing one hut or triggering an advancement.","Acceptance: verify population and staffing map, food and tool reserves, warehouse and courier capacity, production bottlenecks, defence coverage, research priority and recovery after losing one essential service; staff and supply the service, run a representative work cycle, record requests, delivery delay and output, test worker absence or blocked storage, recover without commands and remove material, XP, loot and advancement-reward incentives."]
	quest.23012F6C4C522CEB.quest_desc: ["Settlement Management Checkpoint 2CEB is a settlement systems-design checkpoint in the MineColonies settlement route. The lesson is a staffed, supplied and recoverable civic service with measurable demand and output—not a reward for placing one hut or triggering an advancement.","Acceptance: verify population and staffing map, food and tool reserves, warehouse and courier capacity, production bottlenecks, defence coverage, research priority and recovery after losing one essential service; staff and supply the service, run a representative work cycle, record requests, delivery delay and output, test worker absence or blocked storage, recover without commands and remove material, XP, loot and advancement-reward incentives."]
	quest.230463E830D6FFEB.quest_desc: ["Empty Pcb is a printed-circuit manufacturing component in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify plastic preparation, UV exposure, etching time, acid handling, board yield and prevention of early PCB rewards; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.232F28C7B5A9F4DD.quest_desc: ["Welcome to &#FF2E62MFM&r! This mod is designed to eliminate the grind by turning energy into resources. To get started, you will need a source of Forge Energy (FE) from another mod. Your journey begins with understanding the world around you."]
