	quest.28B88FFE1B735E3E.quest_desc: ["Pumpjack Hammer Part / Pumpjack Hammer Head / Pumpjack Hammer Connector / Super Glue is a specialized TFMG metallurgy component in the TFMG metallurgy route. The lesson must establish repeatable coke, refractory, iron or steel production with measured yield and recoverable multiblocks—not reward the player with the same fuel or metal being requested.","Acceptance: verify its material ancestry, heat and fuel contract, multiblock or fabrication role, measured yield, byproduct route, safe cooldown and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; run a representative heat or casting batch, record fuel, ore, flux, temperature or cycle time, metal and byproducts, test blocked output or fuel loss, cool and recover safely, and remove item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.28DCEC2D45A88C6A.quest_desc: ["Vibranium Mage Helmet / Vibranium Mage Chestplate / Vibranium Mage Leggings / Vibranium Mage Boots is a cross-mod prerequisite or support material for dimensional processing in the Allthemodium resource branch. Its value must come from the assigned dimension, a stage-appropriate extraction method and a documented processing chain—not from a reward that duplicates rare ore, templates or finished equipment.","Acceptance: verify its legal source, assigned stage, exact consumption, replacement policy and why it supports rather than substitutes the dimensional resource chain; record the source dimension and permission, obtain or process one legal batch, measure yield and loss, test storage and restart recovery, protect templates and unique inputs and confirm that rewards, simulated mining, EMC, trade, loot rerolls and duplication cannot create the resource early."]
	quest.28F1702618BF23DD.quest_desc: ["Dragon Stick is a specialized Ice and Fire expedition component in the Ice and Fire progression branch. Its value comes from prepared exploration, first-victory evidence, controlled dragon interaction or a repeatable forge—not from receiving rare materials from the quest book.","Acceptance: verify legal acquisition, encounter or production context, unique-drop policy, safe storage, repeatability and recovery after a failed expedition; document preparation and retreat criteria, complete the encounter or production cycle, reconcile unique and ordinary drops, test one failure or interrupted state and remove reward, loot-reroll, simulation, trade and duplication shortcuts."]
