	quest.3FC7FDAF84871963.quest_desc: ["Reactor Safety Checkpoint 1963 is a reactor and turbine commissioning checkpoint in the Extreme Reactors power branch. It must be accepted as part of a complete, instrumented multiblock whose fuel, heat, waste, coolant and output are reconciled—not as an isolated block or reward-funded power shortcut.","Acceptance: verify structure validation, fuel reserve, moderator or coolant, instrumentation, output load, waste route, control response, shutdown, restart and measured efficiency; build or inspect the complete structure, record a cold baseline, run a bounded fuel batch, measure output and waste, test control-rod or emergency shutdown response, recover after full output or restart and confirm that rewards, duplicated fuel, free coolant and waste loops cannot create net power or gated materials."]
