	quest.407FBBE12EA9ED9B.quest_desc: ["Diesel Engine Cylinder is a electromechanical generation or conversion machine in the TFMG electrical route. The lesson must establish a measured and protected power capability with reproducible conductor and component supply—not reward the player with the same wire, magnet or capacitor being requested.","Acceptance: verify mechanical input or electrical output, rotational speed, sustained generation, load response, startup reserve, idle loss and controlled shutdown under overload; build or operate a representative circuit, record voltage, current or capacity and the limiting component, test overload, empty generation or disconnected output, recover safely and remove material, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.40915337B7E427F8.quest_desc: ["Superconductor Cable is a voltage-tier electrical component in Modern Industrialization. The real requirement is a stable material and machine network with controlled voltage, fluids, byproducts and throughput rather than possession of one block.","Acceptance: verify voltage tier, amperage or EU demand, cable loss, transformer boundary, overvoltage protection and reserve capacity; complete a representative unattended batch, record energy, fluid and material reserves, test full output or power loss, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.40952B7721569DE2.quest_desc: ["Infinity Axe is a specialized Avaritia endgame component in Avaritia. Difficulty must come from mature cross-mod infrastructure, parallel production and controlled convergence rather than repetitive manual crafting or random rewards.","Acceptance: verify its resource-domain dependencies, automation path, effective capability and strict post-stage acquisition policy; demonstrate a repeatable automated supply path, record throughput and reserves, retain reusable permissions, and close loot, reward, EMC, seed, bee, mob-simulation, salvage and alternate-recipe bypasses."]
	quest.40952B7721569DE2.quest_subtitle: "Turns trees into dust. Turns enemies into memories."
	quest.40BEBD299B406E1A.quest_desc: ["Generator is a electromechanical generation or conversion machine in the TFMG electrical route. The lesson must establish a measured and protected power capability with reproducible conductor and component supply—not reward the player with the same wire, magnet or capacitor being requested.","Acceptance: verify mechanical input or electrical output, rotational speed, sustained generation, load response, startup reserve, idle loss and controlled shutdown under overload; build or operate a representative circuit, record voltage, current or capacity and the limiting component, test overload, empty generation or disconnected output, recover safely and remove material, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.40F1315207ADEB80.quest_subtitle: "Allows you to cut and paste any type of build"
	quest.40F634AC38F42B88.quest_desc: ["Pressure Tube is a air-network distribution or safety component in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify tube pressure rating, branch loss, regulator setpoint, isolation valve, leak diagnosis and overpressure protection; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.40F8FF1E85694FD4.quest_desc: ["Copper Wire is a conductor or stock-material fabrication component in the Create Crafts & Additions branch. It must be validated inside a complete conversion or distribution system with known direction, load and losses—not treated as a collectible part whose cost is refunded by quest experience or materials.","Acceptance: verify feedstock identity, rolling or drawing sequence, batch yield, stress and speed requirement, conductor material, buffer limit, scrap handling and reconciliation proving that no metal is multiplied; record an idle baseline, run one bounded batch or power interval, measure input, output and losses, test overload or disconnected-output behavior, recover after shutdown or restart and confirm that rewards, duplicated conductors and free energy feedback cannot bypass the intended infrastructure cost."]
	quest.40F8FF1E85694FD4.quest_subtitle: "Crafting component."
	quest.410077C7B973F318.quest_desc: ["Sorcerer Hood is a magical equipment tier in Ars Nouveau. Its value depends on Source economy, spell configuration, automation behaviour or ritual conditions rather than on possessing the item alone.","Acceptance: verify mana or Source benefit, thread slots, defensive statistics, mobility interaction and repair path; perform a representative spell, ritual or automated cycle, record Source use and recovery, test interruption or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, duplication and alternate-crafting shortcuts."]
	quest.4101F8275B41C79B.quest_desc: ["The 1k Storage Disk can store 1000 items."]
	quest.4101F8275B41C79B.title: "&61k Storage Part&r"
	quest.411C46F666CE2E79.quest_desc: ["Item Wyvern Large Shield Capacity is a specialized Draconic Evolution component in Draconic Evolution. Its true progression value includes energy scale, modules, special abilities and infrastructure requirements rather than only the visible crafting ingredients.","Acceptance: verify its tier, charged state, module or multiblock dependency, effective capability and safe failure state; test the complete charged or operating state, record energy and material reserves, define a recoverable failure procedure, and close loot, reward, trade, EMC, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.413C2915D27F0D99.quest_desc: ["At first glance, it's just a harmless holiday treat. But down here? It's, sticky, and slightly cursed."]
	quest.4181323BF72047A9.quest_desc: ["Schedule is a railway and train-system component in Create. The meaningful requirement is a stable kinetic or logistical system with known speed, stress, direction and failure behaviour rather than ownership of one component.","Acceptance: verify track continuity, station ownership, schedule order, signal blocks, loading time, unloaded chunks and recovery from obstruction; run a representative unattended batch or movement cycle, record RPM, stress and buffers, test blockage or reversal, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4189BC3DFB551F4C.quest_desc: ["Advanced Mekanism Checkpoint 1F4C is a advanced Mekanism system-design checkpoint in the advanced Mekanism ecosystem. Its progression value depends on sustained power, chemical, radiation, heat, transport or modular-equipment infrastructure rather than on possessing one block or item.","Acceptance: verify documented energy tree, chemical and heat loops, radiation containment, digital logistics, emergency shutdown and restart procedure; complete a representative operating cycle, record energy, heat, chemical and material reserves, test blocked output or interrupted power, and close reward, loot, trade, EMC, simulation, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4189BC3DFB551F4C.title: "Advanced Mekanism Checkpoint 1F4C — Advanced-System Acceptance"
	quest.419BBE875D40B1D6.quest_desc: [
		"The ME Export Bus extracts items from the ME Network's Networked Storage and places them into the inventory it faces."
		""
		"You must configure which items it will insert, leaving the configuration blank will result in nothing."
		""
		"The ME Export Bus will try to export any of the items on its list skipping over those it cannot fit into the destination."
		""
		"The ME Export Bus&r requires a Channel to function."
		""
		"This is the functional opposite of the ME Import Bus."
	]
	quest.419DD6FE84B91749.quest_subtitle: "Mixes the matching genes"
	quest.41A3DDA294728106.quest_desc: ["Create S&A Field-Test Checkpoint 8106 is a Create S&A system-design checkpoint in the Create Stuff & Additions branch. It must be evaluated as part of a powered mechanical system with explicit fuel, stress, range or durability limits—not as a collectible item whose quest reward refunds its cost.","Acceptance: verify energy source, stress budget, operator safety, mobility limits, tool permissions, maintenance stock, shutdown behavior and post-failure recovery; document inputs and idle state, run one representative work cycle, measure consumption or operating duration, test blocked-output or low-power behavior, recover after interruption and confirm that quest rewards, duplicated fuel and free replacement parts cannot bypass the intended cost."]
	quest.41AED1C20749E824.quest_desc: ["Infinite Logistical Transporter is a tiered transport-network component in the advanced Mekanism ecosystem. Its progression value depends on sustained power, chemical, radiation, heat, transport or modular-equipment infrastructure rather than on possessing one block or item.","Acceptance: verify transferred medium, throughput, pull-push direction, colour or diversion rules, network capacity and loop isolation; complete a representative operating cycle, record energy, heat, chemical and material reserves, test blocked output or interrupted power, and close reward, loot, trade, EMC, simulation, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.41D1344A31FEA6DF.quest_desc: ["Kanthal Coil is a machine-structure or electromechanical component in Modern Industrialization. The real requirement is a stable material and machine network with controlled voltage, fluids, byproducts and throughput rather than possession of one block.","Acceptance: verify previous-tier ancestry, material forms, motor or pump tier, reusable molds and continuous component stocking; complete a representative unattended batch, record energy, fluid and material reserves, test full output or power loss, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.41E91ED150046688.quest_subtitle: "You can use Mystical Agriculture!"
	quest.41EB0C570FC54F43.quest_desc: ["Basic Chemical Tank is a chemical, gas or fluid-processing component in the first Mekanism production era. It matters only when its energy, material, chemical, transport and side-configuration contract is understood and connected to a repeatable factory.","Acceptance: verify phase identity, tank ownership, dump policy, secondary inputs, conversion ratio, contamination prevention and a clean purge before recipe changes; run a representative batch, record input, output, energy and internal-buffer behaviour, test blocked output or power loss, and remove reward, EMC, loot, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.41F93E64432175D5.quest_desc: ["Treated Fence / Sheetmetal Iron is a specialized Immersive Engineering component in the Immersive Engineering route. The objective is a measurable, serviceable industrial capability with legal inputs and recoverable failure—not a random reward for crafting one block or tool.","Acceptance: verify its exact industrial role, material ancestry, power or fuel demand, interface, representative cycle, failure state and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; build or operate a representative installation, record input, output, power or fuel and limiting section, test blocked output or loss of supply, recover safely and remove random-table, item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.41F93E64432175D5.quest_subtitle: "The Tank is a 3x3x5 multi-block used for storing liquids"
	quest.41F93E64432175D5.title: "Treated Fence / Sheetmetal Iron — Industrial Acceptance"
	quest.4204702AA6FBF40B.quest_desc: ["Chargepad is a specialized early Mekanism component in the first Mekanism production era. It matters only when its energy, material, chemical, transport and side-configuration contract is understood and connected to a repeatable factory.","Acceptance: verify its exact input-output contract, power demand, configuration, integration point, repeat batch and safe blocked state; run a representative batch, record input, output, energy and internal-buffer behaviour, test blocked output or power loss, and remove reward, EMC, loot, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.42125A0E7E0AAFAF.quest_desc: ["Ufo Helmet / Ufo Chestplate / Ufo Leggings / Ufo Boots is a cross-mod space-mission support component in the Stellaris space-engineering route. Its progression value depends on a documented material, life-support, propulsion, power or mission contract—not on receiving a spacecraft component from a quest reward.","Acceptance: verify which system owns production, storage, power, communication or recovery and why it supports the mission without granting an early destination or protected resource; produce or operate a representative unit, record mass or stock, energy, fuel, oxygen and recovery reserves, test one aborted or interrupted state and remove reward, trade, loot, duplication and early-planet shortcuts."]
	quest.42125A0E7E0AAFAF.quest_subtitle: "Not for long..."
	quest.421851D4D39910DB.quest_desc: ["Apiary Checkpoint 10DB is a specialized Productive Bees production component in the Productive Bees route. The objective is a healthy, supplied and recoverable production cell—not collecting a comb or receiving a bee from a quest reward.","Acceptance: verify its exact hive, breeding, processing, genetics or logistics role, legal source, representative operating cycle, finite buffer and recovery after one bee or machine becomes unavailable; run or observe a representative production cycle, record hive occupancy, environmental condition, comb rate, processing output and overflow, then test one interruption without losing a rare bee."]
	quest.421851D4D39910DB.title: "Apiary Checkpoint 10DB — Apiary Acceptance"
	quest.42195C45933ACA1E.quest_desc: ["Welcome to Create: Central Kitchen, a mod offering more tools and methods to automate food processing for other mods in Create."]
	quest.421EA2CE61003DA1.quest_desc: ["Andesite Jetpack Chestplate is a powered mobility or wearable engineering system in the Create Stuff & Additions branch. It must be evaluated as part of a powered mechanical system with explicit fuel, stress, range or durability limits—not as a collectible item whose quest reward refunds its cost.","Acceptance: verify fuel or charge route, operating duration, fall and void safety, armor trade-off, emergency landing, repair path and restrictions in staged exploration or boss encounters; document inputs and idle state, run one representative work cycle, measure consumption or operating duration, test blocked-output or low-power behavior, recover after interruption and confirm that quest rewards, duplicated fuel and free replacement parts cannot bypass the intended cost."]
	quest.4236B9F071BE18F3.quest_desc: ["Rotary Condensentrator is a chemical, gas or fluid-processing component in the first Mekanism production era. It matters only when its energy, material, chemical, transport and side-configuration contract is understood and connected to a repeatable factory.","Acceptance: verify phase identity, tank ownership, dump policy, secondary inputs, conversion ratio, contamination prevention and a clean purge before recipe changes; run a representative batch, record input, output, energy and internal-buffer behaviour, test blocked output or power loss, and remove reward, EMC, loot, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4266BF7FCE3B4330.quest_desc: ["Cogwheel / Large Cogwheel is a kinetic transmission component in Create. The meaningful requirement is a stable kinetic or logistical system with known speed, stress, direction and failure behaviour rather than ownership of one component.","Acceptance: verify rotation direction, RPM ratio, stress capacity, branch isolation, reverse state and visible diagnostics; run a representative unattended batch or movement cycle, record RPM, stress and buffers, test blockage or reversal, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4266BF7FCE3B4330.title: "Cogwheel / Large Cogwheel — Kinetic Acceptance"
	quest.4276B941670CE0E2.quest_desc: [
		"P2P tunnels are a way to move things like items, fluids, redstone signals, power, light, and channels around a network without them directly interacting with the network. There are many variants of P2P tunnel but each only transports its specific type of thing. They essentially act like portals that directly connect two block faces at range. They are not bi-directional, there are defined inputs and outputs."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"There are many types of P2P tunnel. Only the ME P2P tunnel is directly craftable, the others are made by right-clicking other P2P tunnels with certain items:"
		""
		"ME P2P tunnels are selected by right-clicking with any cable."
		"Redstone P2P tunnels are selected by right-clicking with a variety of redstone components."
		"Item P2P tunnels are selected by right-clicking with a chest or hopper."
		"Fluid P2P tunnels are selected by right-clicking with a bucket or bottle."
		"Energy P2P tunnels are selected by right-clicking with almost any energy-containing item."
		"Light P2P tunnels are selected by right-clicking with a torch or glowstone"
		"Some tunnel types have quirks. For instance, ME P2P tunnels' channels cannot pass through other ME P2P tunnels, and Energy P2P tunnels indirectly extract a 2.5% tax on FE flowing through themselves by increasing their energy draw."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"The most common use case of P2P tunnels is using a ME P2P tunnel to compact the density of channel transport. Instead of a bundle of dense cable, a single dense cable can be used to carry many channels around."
	]
	quest.4291A72FF87220D5.quest_desc: [
		"There is also an inverted version of the toggle bus that &ndisables&r the connection when a &credstone&r signal is supplied."
		""
		"When &credstone&r signal supplied the part &nenables&r the connection, &6ME Inverted Toggle Bus&r provides the &nreverse&r behavior by &ndisabling&r the connection instead."
	]
	quest.42951D14ADCD9332.quest_desc: ["Cod N Chips is a specialized PneumaticCraft component in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify its pressure, heat, air, program or logistics contract and a safe blocked, empty or overpressure state; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.42A3D1BBCF05AEF9.quest_desc: ["Creative Fluid Tank is a infinite item, fluid or chemical storage permission granted only after creative convergence. Ownership is not sufficient proof: the item must have an authoritative multi-branch recipe, no alternative acquisition route and an explicit operating policy that prevents infinite output from bypassing protected resources, dimensions, encounters or progression permissions.","Acceptance: verify configured resource identity, insertion and extraction policy, filter locking, protected-resource blacklist, void and overflow behavior, automation access, restart persistence and confirmation that unique or gated resources cannot be configured; trace the complete recipe ancestry through prior milestones, confirm EMC, simulation, loot, trade and reward blacklists, run one bounded functional test, test full-output or disconnected behavior, document safe storage and restart recovery and prove that the creative capability cannot generate unique drops, first-acquisition evidence or gated crafting permissions."]
	quest.42BF0D7E017F718B.quest_desc: ["Fluix Crystal is a crystal and network-material production step in an AE2 system. The item is useful only when its power, channel, storage and routing assumptions are explicit and the network remains diagnosable under load.","Acceptance: verify crystal source, charging or growth time, batch buffer and contamination-free conversion; run a representative automated job, record channel and power use, test a full or disconnected destination, and prove that loot, rewards, trades or alternate recipes cannot unlock this capability before its stage."]
	quest.42CBFE605060FF20.quest_desc: ["Copper Cell / Copper Pylon / Copper Plinth / Export is a factory multiblock foundation. A Woot factory may reproduce ordinary drops after legitimate progression, but it must never replace first discovery, boss mastery or unique capability rewards.","Acceptance: verify validated layout, controller and heart placement, tier matching, chunk boundaries, restart state and safe disassembly; run a representative bounded batch, record power, consumables, cycle time and output, and prove that random quest rewards, alternate shards, spawner data, EMC, neural models or loot-table aliases cannot automate a restricted encounter."]
	quest.42CBFE605060FF20.title: "Copper Cell / Copper Pylon / Copper Plinth / Export — Factory Legitimacy"
	quest.42D6CC67AB29D7DA.quest_desc: ["Digital Circuit is a industrial control-circuit tier in Modern Industrialization. The real requirement is a stable material and machine network with controlled voltage, fluids, byproducts and throughput rather than possession of one block.","Acceptance: verify previous circuit tier, board and wire supply, clean-room or machine requirement, batch yield and stage authority; complete a representative unattended batch, record energy, fluid and material reserves, test full output or power loss, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.42D7C8CD8E6F5CD7.quest_desc: ["&e- 20 Max Spawn Delay&r - faster spawns."]
	quest.42DF944251E8538F.quest_desc: ["Neutron Collector is a neutronium production component in Avaritia. Difficulty must come from mature cross-mod infrastructure, parallel production and controlled convergence rather than repetitive manual crafting or random rewards.","Acceptance: verify collector count, passive production rate, chunk availability, buffer capacity and fair scaling without manual waiting; demonstrate a repeatable automated supply path, record throughput and reserves, retain reusable permissions, and close loot, reward, EMC, seed, bee, mob-simulation, salvage and alternate-recipe bypasses."]
	quest.42F50CE7FE715583.quest_desc: [" "]
	quest.42F50CE7FE715583.title: "&aUpgrading Our Magical Storage&r"
	quest.430475E11D259B74.quest_desc: ["Settlement Management Checkpoint 9B74 is a settlement systems-design checkpoint in the MineColonies settlement route. The lesson is a staffed, supplied and recoverable civic service with measurable demand and output—not a reward for placing one hut or triggering an advancement.","Acceptance: verify population and staffing map, food and tool reserves, warehouse and courier capacity, production bottlenecks, defence coverage, research priority and recovery after losing one essential service; staff and supply the service, run a representative work cycle, record requests, delivery delay and output, test worker absence or blocked storage, recover without commands and remove material, XP, loot and advancement-reward incentives."]
	quest.430475E11D259B74.quest_subtitle: "Build a Stone Smelter"
	quest.436231715C11E3BA.quest_desc: ["Scattered across the wilds, small bands of Illagers set up camp beneath their distinctive purple tents. Though their supplies are meager and their loot scarce, their presence is a warning, the Illagers’ reach grows wider with every outpost."]
	quest.436231715C11E3BA.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Campsite"
	quest.4378B53C7BB2D518.quest_desc: [
		"To begin generating massive amounts"
		"of power, &aShift + Right-Click&r an &eEternal"
		"Generator&r with an &5Motorola&r to link"
		"them. Once linked, place the &5Motorola&r"
		"into a &4Pandora's Box&r."
		""
		"The &4Pandora's Box&r will then bleed off"
		"the \"overload\" from all linked Eternal"
		"&9Generators&r every minute. Each unit of"
		"overload grants a permanent"
		"generation increase of &e1 FE/t&r."
		"Additionally, you can further boost"
		"energy production by supplying XP"
		"directly into the &4Pandora's Box&r."
	]
	quest.4378B53C7BB2D518.quest_subtitle: "The Ultimate Energy Solution"
	quest.439600B9E9FC5C6E.quest_desc: ["Construction Sticks is a cross-mod support item used in a utility workflow selected for a practical cross-mod workflow. The quest must explain the problem it solves, the resource or energy cost and the situations where it should not be used, rather than treating ownership as proof of mastery.","Acceptance: verify its support role, legal acquisition stage, interaction with the primary utility, replacement policy and confirmation that it does not create free resources or permissions; demonstrate one useful scenario and one misuse or failure case, measure range, capacity, speed or cost where applicable, document cleanup and recovery and confirm that the utility cannot bypass stage permissions, first encounters, protected areas or production requirements."]
	quest.439600B9E9FC5C6E.title: "Construction Sticks — Practical Utility Acceptance"
	quest.439AB4ACFC0FF768.title: "Iesnium Sacrificial Bowl / Dark Iesnium Sacrificial Bowl — Ritual Acceptance"
	quest.439C6C61A5263D31.quest_desc: [
		"Go to the Bedrock level."
		""
		"Place a obsidian above it, leaving one block space in between."
		""
		"Throw as much redstone dust in the gap left by the Bedrock and Obsidian as you want."
		""
		"Left-click the Obsidian. The Obsidian will crush the Redstone Dust against the Bedrock and create Flux!"
	]
	quest.439C6C61A5263D31.quest_subtitle: "Flux Networks lets you send, receive, and store energy across dimensions without cables."
