	quest.442BB17AE7AC4936.quest_desc: ["Infinity Ingot is a cross-mod convergence prerequisite for a creative permission granted only after creative convergence. Ownership is not sufficient proof: the item must have an authoritative multi-branch recipe, no alternative acquisition route and an explicit operating policy that prevents infinite output from bypassing protected resources, dimensions, encounters or progression permissions.","Acceptance: verify its source progression, assigned prior milestone, exact irreversible consumption, blacklist coverage and proof that the creative item cannot refund or recreate the prerequisite; trace the complete recipe ancestry through prior milestones, confirm EMC, simulation, loot, trade and reward blacklists, run one bounded functional test, test full-output or disconnected behavior, document safe storage and restart recovery and prove that the creative capability cannot generate unique drops, first-acquisition evidence or gated crafting permissions."]
	quest.4431F1144F0C5C0C.quest_desc: ["Crystal Matrix Ingot is a endgame structural material in Avaritia. Difficulty must come from mature cross-mod infrastructure, parallel production and controlled convergence rather than repetitive manual crafting or random rewards.","Acceptance: verify full convergence recipe, previous-tier components, antimatter or draconic dependencies, EMC zeroing and scalable batch production; demonstrate a repeatable automated supply path, record throughput and reserves, retain reusable permissions, and close loot, reward, EMC, seed, bee, mob-simulation, salvage and alternate-recipe bypasses."]
	quest.4434D7B66521D69A.quest_desc: ["Basic Pressurized Tube is a Mekanism transport or configuration component in the first Mekanism production era. It matters only when its energy, material, chemical, transport and side-configuration contract is understood and connected to a repeatable factory.","Acceptance: verify transferred medium, pull-push direction, colour or diversion rules, throughput, network capacity, loop isolation and recovery after one segment is removed; run a representative batch, record input, output, energy and internal-buffer behaviour, test blocked output or power loss, and remove reward, EMC, loot, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4434D7B66521D69A.title: "Basic Pressurized Tube — Operating Acceptance"
	quest.445ACC0E40DB3D96.quest_desc: ["Unfinished Resistor is a measurement, regulation or circuit-control component in the TFMG electrical route. The lesson must establish a measured and protected power capability with reproducible conductor and component supply—not reward the player with the same wire, magnet or capacitor being requested.","Acceptance: verify measured quantity and range, probe location, expected reading, regulation rule, safe default, visible fault and calibration against a known operating state; build or operate a representative circuit, record voltage, current or capacity and the limiting component, test overload, empty generation or disconnected output, recover safely and remove material, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.4487635C822086E0.quest_desc: ["Using &bIce shards&r from &cmars&r ore, these machine will generate &bCryofuel&r, a more efficient fuel source then &6oil.&r"]
	quest.44881E39AB1D62AA.quest_desc: ["The &9Crafter&r is how we store patterns for our Network to know how to craft items. Once a recipe is placed into the crafter, you'll be able to 'Request' an item to be crafted from your Grid. You can do this by hitting CTRL+Shift when clicking on the item you have a recipe for to bring up the crafting GUI. \\\\n \\\\n This block can also be placed facing a machine to use &6Processing Patterns&r. For example, if you point the Crafter at a Furnace, you can put a recipe inside for a recipe you need a furnace for, like smelting raw processors. As long as the crafter is attached to your system and the Furnace has an importer attached to it, the Crafter will allow you to request the smelted version of the Processor!"]
	quest.44881E39AB1D62AA.quest_subtitle: "Automated crafting!"
	quest.44881E39AB1D62AA.title: "Crafter"
	quest.4489EFA2FFA1584C.quest_desc: ["Another rocket that allows you to reach more planets"]
	quest.449C41A3AFBBE8E9.quest_desc: ["Blastbrick is a coke, alloy or steel-production material and structure in the Immersive Engineering route. The objective is a measurable, serviceable industrial capability with legal inputs and recoverable failure—not a random reward for crafting one block or tool.","Acceptance: verify complete multiblock counts, fuel and ore ancestry, coke and creosote or slag routes, batch yield, heat-up loss, full-output shutdown and safe cooling before maintenance; build or operate a representative installation, record input, output, power or fuel and limiting section, test blocked output or loss of supply, recover safely and remove random-table, item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.449C41A3AFBBE8E9.title: "Blastbrick — Industrial Acceptance"
	quest.449FA7FE3CBD2102.title: "Netherite Cell / Netherite Pylon / Netherite Plinth — Factory Legitimacy"
	quest.44B0E00B7465F278.quest_desc: ["Enchanters Shield is a specialized Ars Nouveau component in Ars Nouveau. Its value depends on Source economy, spell configuration, automation behaviour or ritual conditions rather than on possessing the item alone.","Acceptance: verify its Source, spell, ritual, entity or automation contract and a safe invalid-input or interrupted state; perform a representative spell, ritual or automated cycle, record Source use and recovery, test interruption or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, duplication and alternate-crafting shortcuts."]
	quest.44B1B147CDAC4E36.quest_desc: ["This gives X-Ray vision for mobs, highlighting them from afar to make it easier to spot them."]
	quest.44CD6DD20F51123F.quest_desc: ["Staff Of Travelling is a travel and teleportation component in Ender IO. Its value comes from alloy processing, conduit topology, capacitor tier or machine configuration rather than from owning the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify destination ownership, range or dimensional rule, energy cost, safe arrival and recovery from a lost anchor; complete a representative unattended cycle, record energy and material reserves, test a blocked output or disconnected conduit, and close loot, reward, trade, spawner, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.44D115281B0BFB75.quest_desc: ["Whispers speak of a &9flying vessel&r that hovers above the world, shimmering with strange energy. Few dare approach, for those who return tell of eerie lights, warped corridors, and guardians not of this realm. Seek it out, if you dare—and uncover the secrets hidden within its metallic shell."]
	quest.44D115281B0BFB75.quest_subtitle: "Find a Giant Mushroom"
	quest.44DA7BE0F0E3E529.quest_subtitle: "The Nether!"
	quest.44DA7BE0F0E3E529.title: "Survival Workshop Checkpoint E529 — Foundation Acceptance"
	quest.44E8D5277063565A.quest_desc: ["Voltage Observer is a specialized TFMG chemical component in the TFMG chemical route. The lesson must establish a contained, measurable and repeatable process with legal feedstock and byproduct handling—not reward the player with the same acid, plastic or metal being requested.","Acceptance: verify its legal feedstock, phase, reaction or separation contract, containment, measurable yield, byproduct path, safe purge and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; run a representative reaction or separation batch, record feedstock, ratio, temperature or pressure, output and byproducts, test blocked output or contamination, purge safely and remove item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.4512B97451C2221F.quest_desc: ["Mechanical Arm is a factory sensing or control component in Create. The meaningful requirement is a stable kinetic or logistical system with known speed, stress, direction and failure behaviour rather than ownership of one component.","Acceptance: verify input signal, target selection, priority, stock threshold, wireless channel ownership and safe default state; run a representative unattended batch or movement cycle, record RPM, stress and buffers, test blockage or reversal, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.451517C833D25E1A.quest_desc: ["Crafting Core is a specialized Draconic Evolution component in Draconic Evolution. Its true progression value includes energy scale, modules, special abilities and infrastructure requirements rather than only the visible crafting ingredients.","Acceptance: verify its tier, charged state, module or multiblock dependency, effective capability and safe failure state; test the complete charged or operating state, record energy and material reserves, define a recoverable failure procedure, and close loot, reward, trade, EMC, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.453B1A596BE686ED.quest_desc: ["Flux Crafter is a tiered Extended Crafting package executor in the Packaged Automation branch. It must execute an explicit recipe contract with complete inputs, a single accountable output and deterministic recovery—not act as a shortcut whose quest reward supplies black iron, awakened material or cosmic components.","Acceptance: verify supported crafting tier, encoded-grid size, energy and time cost, package throughput, catalyst handling, output identity, parallel-job limit and rejection of recipes above the assigned progression stage; encode one representative recipe, submit exactly one bounded input set, reconcile package contents and final output, test missing-input, full-output and restart states, recover every retained item and confirm that rewards, duplicate packages, recursive unpacking and parallel endpoint races cannot create extra material."]
	quest.453B1A596BE686ED.title: "Flux Crafter — Atomic Automation Acceptance"
	quest.453C36B78EB4B311.quest_desc: ["Salvaging Table is a affix reforging or material-recovery station in the Apotheosis progression system. It must be treated as a controlled upgrade or encounter tool whose value comes from measured build improvement, recoverable materials and explicit risk—not from a quest reward that skips the affix economy.","Acceptance: verify input rarity, material tier, deterministic costs, rejected-result recovery, output comparison and a bounded reroll policy that cannot consume unlimited resources silently; record the before-and-after equipment state, resource cost and failure condition, test one representative combat or enchanting cycle, salvage or recover rejected results and confirm that rewards, rerolls, duplication and unrestricted boss spawning cannot bypass the intended progression."]
	quest.454812A6E386C6D0.quest_subtitle: "sneaky sneaky, they can't find this subtitle"
	quest.454F315FF637EA84.quest_subtitle: "Big Patter Storage!!"
	quest.454FF6E2926163F7.quest_desc: ["MI Factory Checkpoint 63F7 is a industrial-factory design checkpoint in Modern Industrialization. The real requirement is a stable material and machine network with controlled voltage, fluids, byproducts and throughput rather than possession of one block.","Acceptance: verify documented voltage tree, steam and fluid budgets, component stock, byproduct routing, failure isolation and restart procedure; complete a representative unattended batch, record energy, fluid and material reserves, test full output or power loss, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4561FE8367CD8216.quest_desc: ["Item Draconic Proj Anti Immune is a specialized Draconic Evolution component in Draconic Evolution. Its true progression value includes energy scale, modules, special abilities and infrastructure requirements rather than only the visible crafting ingredients.","Acceptance: verify its tier, charged state, module or multiblock dependency, effective capability and safe failure state; test the complete charged or operating state, record energy and material reserves, define a recoverable failure procedure, and close loot, reward, trade, EMC, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.456E6532B7FBA2EA.quest_subtitle: "\"The power of the sun in the palm of my hands.\""
	quest.459AA2AD67CA6AAA.quest_desc: ["Thermite Powder is a specialized TFMG chemical component in the TFMG chemical route. The lesson must establish a contained, measurable and repeatable process with legal feedstock and byproduct handling—not reward the player with the same acid, plastic or metal being requested.","Acceptance: verify its legal feedstock, phase, reaction or separation contract, containment, measurable yield, byproduct path, safe purge and repeatable replacement from current-stage infrastructure; run a representative reaction or separation batch, record feedstock, ratio, temperature or pressure, output and byproducts, test blocked output or contamination, purge safely and remove item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.45B26D389684EF9B.quest_desc: ["Cosmic Thermodynamic Conductor is a tiered transport-network component in the advanced Mekanism ecosystem. Its progression value depends on sustained power, chemical, radiation, heat, transport or modular-equipment infrastructure rather than on possessing one block or item.","Acceptance: verify transferred medium, throughput, pull-push direction, colour or diversion rules, network capacity and loop isolation; complete a representative operating cycle, record energy, heat, chemical and material reserves, test blocked output or interrupted power, and close reward, loot, trade, EMC, simulation, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.45BA5B8A785E1B82.quest_desc: ["Wrench is a configuration, diagnostic or planning tool in Create. The meaningful requirement is a stable kinetic or logistical system with known speed, stress, direction and failure behaviour rather than ownership of one component.","Acceptance: verify exact configuration effect, copied data, ownership, safe reset, replacement after loss and use in diagnosing the production line; run a representative unattended batch or movement cycle, record RPM, stress and buffers, test blockage or reversal, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.45C02BA617A092FC.quest_desc: ["Pumpjack is a specialized Stellaris mission component in the Stellaris expedition branch. It must be validated as part of a complete mission architecture with power, atmosphere, supplies, transport and recovery—not as an isolated item whose resource cost is refunded by the quest book.","Acceptance: verify mission role, staged source, power or material cost, operating envelope, environmental hazard, reserve margin, failure recovery and safe return; document mission inputs and reserve margins, run one representative operating interval or launch cycle, measure consumption and output, test a low-power, low-supply or disconnected state, complete safe shutdown or return and confirm that rewards, duplicated fuel, free atmosphere and teleport shortcuts cannot bypass expedition progression."]
	quest.45CEF843FA33853F.quest_desc: ["Block Picker is a specialized Create Stuff & Additions device in the Create Stuff & Additions branch. It must be evaluated as part of a powered mechanical system with explicit fuel, stress, range or durability limits—not as a collectible item whose quest reward refunds its cost.","Acceptance: verify power source, material cost, operating limit, useful work rate, failure mode, recovery and integration with current-stage Create infrastructure; document inputs and idle state, run one representative work cycle, measure consumption or operating duration, test blocked-output or low-power behavior, recover after interruption and confirm that quest rewards, duplicated fuel and free replacement parts cannot bypass the intended cost."]
	quest.45D20904723662F8.quest_desc: [
		"You cannot replicate what you do not understand. Take your Scanner and use it on a mob (Right-Click). This will add the entity's data to your personal &a&lPlayer Index&r."
