	quest.4F09E98E5E615AC9.title: "Redstone Transmitter / Redstone Receiver — Infrastructure Acceptance"
	quest.4F1307BB5B01F90F.quest_desc: [
		"The ME Chest acts like a miniature network with a ME Terminal, ME Drive, and Energy Acceptor. While it can be used as a tiny storage network, its capacity for just one single storage cell means it has limited utility as such."
		""
		"Instead, it is useful for interacting with specifically the storage cell mounted inside it. Its integrated terminal can only see and access the items in the mounted drive, while devices on the general network can access items in any network storage, including ME chests."
		""
		"It has 2 different GUIs and is sided for item transport. Interacting with the top terminal opens the integrated terminal. Items can be inserted into the mounted storage cell through this face, but not extracted. Interacting with any other face opens the GUI with the slot for the storage cell and the priority settings. The cell can be inserted and removed by item logistics only through the face with the cell slot."
		""
		"It can be rotated with a Certus Quartz Wrench."
		""
		"It has a small AE energy storage buffer, so if not on a network with an energy cell, inserting or extracting too many items at once may cause it to brown out."
	]
	quest.4F1C04C0F6769825.quest_desc: ["Chemical Injection Chamber is a primary ore or material-processing machine in the first Mekanism production era. It matters only when its energy, material, chemical, transport and side-configuration contract is understood and connected to a repeatable factory.","Acceptance: verify recipe ownership, exact yield, secondary or infusion input, energy per batch, side configuration, output separation and shutdown under a full destination; run a representative batch, record input, output, energy and internal-buffer behaviour, test blocked output or power loss, and remove reward, EMC, loot, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.4F1C04C0F6769825.title: "Chemical Injection Chamber — Operating Acceptance"
	quest.4F1FA866A2F510A1.quest_desc: ["Electrum Rod is a conductor or stock-material fabrication component in the Create Crafts & Additions branch. It must be validated inside a complete conversion or distribution system with known direction, load and losses—not treated as a collectible part whose cost is refunded by quest experience or materials.","Acceptance: verify feedstock identity, rolling or drawing sequence, batch yield, stress and speed requirement, conductor material, buffer limit, scrap handling and reconciliation proving that no metal is multiplied; record an idle baseline, run one bounded batch or power interval, measure input, output and losses, test overload or disconnected-output behavior, recover after shutdown or restart and confirm that rewards, duplicated conductors and free energy feedback cannot bypass the intended infrastructure cost."]
	quest.4F1FA866A2F510A1.quest_subtitle: "Crafting component."
	quest.4F216AB740548F80.quest_desc: ["Large Engine is a electromechanical generation or conversion machine in the TFMG electrical route. The lesson must establish a measured and protected power capability with reproducible conductor and component supply—not reward the player with the same wire, magnet or capacitor being requested.","Acceptance: verify mechanical input or electrical output, rotational speed, sustained generation, load response, startup reserve, idle loss and controlled shutdown under overload; build or operate a representative circuit, record voltage, current or capacity and the limiting component, test overload, empty generation or disconnected output, recover safely and remove material, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.4F2F6E31C38DA17F.quest_desc: ["Medium Filling Tank is a specialized Create Stuff & Additions device in the Create Stuff & Additions branch. It must be evaluated as part of a powered mechanical system with explicit fuel, stress, range or durability limits—not as a collectible item whose quest reward refunds its cost.","Acceptance: verify power source, material cost, operating limit, useful work rate, failure mode, recovery and integration with current-stage Create infrastructure; document inputs and idle state, run one representative work cycle, measure consumption or operating duration, test blocked-output or low-power behavior, recover after interruption and confirm that quest rewards, duplicated fuel and free replacement parts cannot bypass the intended cost."]
	quest.4F30FA10742473D3.quest_desc: [
		"After using a &aheavyweight&r to create this, you will need a build a &dmagnetic quarry&r to use it."
		""
		"&lFirst:&r craft &bfour magnetic lights&r and place them in a &esquare perimater&r."
		""
		"&lSecond:&r Place down a &cMagnetic quarry&r crafted from the &bheart of iron&r next to the perimeter of &bmagnetic lights&r."
		""
		"&lFinally:&r Place the &cQuarry smasher&r in the &emiddle&r of the square and &dwatch it mine!&r"
	]
