	quest.5A2174711D9219BF.quest_desc: ["Utility Review Checkpoint 19BF is a utility-selection and safety checkpoint selected for a practical cross-mod workflow. The quest must explain the problem it solves, the resource or energy cost and the situations where it should not be used, rather than treating ownership as proof of mastery.","Acceptance: verify the original problem, chosen tool, measurable benefit, operating cost, unsafe use, rollback, maintenance and whether a simpler stage-appropriate solution is preferable; demonstrate one useful scenario and one misuse or failure case, measure range, capacity, speed or cost where applicable, document cleanup and recovery and confirm that the utility cannot bypass stage permissions, first encounters, protected areas or production requirements."]
	quest.5A2450162FD24F7E.quest_desc: ["Crushing Wheel is a kinetic processing machine in Create. The meaningful requirement is a stable kinetic or logistical system with known speed, stress, direction and failure behaviour rather than ownership of one component.","Acceptance: verify required RPM and stress, recipe isolation, input and output buffer, heat or fluid condition, byproducts and full-output shutdown; run a representative unattended batch or movement cycle, record RPM, stress and buffers, test blockage or reversal, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.5A2450162FD24F7E.quest_subtitle: "Crushing Wheels applie Crushing recipes to any items inserted from the direction they are spinning away from."
	quest.5A2450162FD24F7E.title: "Crushing Wheel — Kinetic Acceptance"
	quest.5A26E1BB8C1B8172.quest_desc: ["Solar Panel Starter is a Starter daylight generator in the Powah energy chain. Its tier is meaningful only when the upstream energizing materials and the downstream machine or network can operate at the same sustained rate.","Acceptance: verify day-night duty cycle, sky access and storage reserve; run a representative load without manual inventory correction, record input/output rate and reserve, and prove that quest rewards, EMC, trades or alternate recipes cannot unlock this tier early."]
	quest.5A2AF10773FA8B2D.quest_desc: ["Modular Router / Sender Module 1 / Puller Module 1 is a cross-mod support item used in a utility workflow selected for a practical cross-mod workflow. The quest must explain the problem it solves, the resource or energy cost and the situations where it should not be used, rather than treating ownership as proof of mastery.","Acceptance: verify its support role, legal acquisition stage, interaction with the primary utility, replacement policy and confirmation that it does not create free resources or permissions; demonstrate one useful scenario and one misuse or failure case, measure range, capacity, speed or cost where applicable, document cleanup and recovery and confirm that the utility cannot bypass stage permissions, first encounters, protected areas or production requirements."]
	quest.5A3D5CAD827CCCB8.quest_desc: [
		"You’ve tasted the chaos, battled the sweets, and survived the cavity. You’ve earned your sugar high."
		""
		"&dThis effect can be obtained by eating any candy from the candy cavity, with the sundae being the most likely to grant this effect&f."
	]
	quest.5A58D4B25C9CB757.quest_desc: ["Awakened Supremium Sword / Awakened Supremium Pickaxe / Awakened Supremium Axe / System is a linked agriculture system. In an expert progression pack, renewable production is permitted only after the represented resource, creature or capability has been obtained through its legitimate stage path.","Acceptance: verify component ratios, shared catalysts, legal crop tiers, output ownership and unattended completion without duplicating seeds or essences; process or harvest a representative batch with bounded automation, record yield and reserve, and prove that quest rewards, EMC, trades, loot, simulated mobs or alternate seed recipes cannot unlock or multiply this resource early."]
	quest.5A5A30CD4D0C98CB.quest_desc: ["Fluix Crystal is crafted in world by tossing Charged Certus Quartz Crystal, Nether Quartz and Redstone Dust in Water."]
	quest.5A615BB74A5CD332.quest_desc: ["Ludicrite Ingot / Ridiculite Ingot is a reactor fuel or structural feedstock in the Extreme Reactors power branch. It must be accepted as part of a complete, instrumented multiblock whose fuel, heat, waste, coolant and output are reconciled—not as an isolated block or reward-funded power shortcut.","Acceptance: verify legal ore source, processing yield, fuel composition, batch mass, storage limit, consumption rate and prohibition on quest rewards or recycling creating more fresh fuel than was consumed; build or inspect the complete structure, record a cold baseline, run a bounded fuel batch, measure output and waste, test control-rod or emergency shutdown response, recover after full output or restart and confirm that rewards, duplicated fuel, free coolant and waste loops cannot create net power or gated materials."]
	quest.5A70A9C0D6D77639.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.5A9B2246E33065A5.quest_desc: ["Apiary Checkpoint 65A5 is a specialized Productive Bees production component in the Productive Bees route. The objective is a healthy, supplied and recoverable production cell—not collecting a comb or receiving a bee from a quest reward.","Acceptance: verify its exact hive, breeding, processing, genetics or logistics role, legal source, representative operating cycle, finite buffer and recovery after one bee or machine becomes unavailable; run or observe a representative production cycle, record hive occupancy, environmental condition, comb rate, processing output and overflow, then test one interruption without losing a rare bee."]
	quest.5A9B2246E33065A5.title: "Apiary Checkpoint 65A5 — Apiary Acceptance"
	quest.5A9D6672385D3D82.quest_desc: ["Upgrade Matrix is a machine or equipment upgrade in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify compatible host, stack limit, additional pressure or air demand, exact capability gain and safe removal; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.5AAFDED22803AE85.quest_subtitle: "Contains some useful info"
	quest.5ACF4B46ED9134B2.quest_desc: ["Vibranium Helmet / Vibranium Chestplate / Vibranium Leggings / Vibranium Boots is a dimensional-metal equipment or tool in the Allthemodium resource branch. Its value must come from the assigned dimension, a stage-appropriate extraction method and a documented processing chain—not from a reward that duplicates rare ore, templates or finished equipment.","Acceptance: verify material and template ancestry, smithing sequence, durability and repair route, measured benefit over current-stage gear, special effects and prevention of the item trivializing later permissions; record the source dimension and permission, obtain or process one legal batch, measure yield and loss, test storage and restart recovery, protect templates and unique inputs and confirm that rewards, simulated mining, EMC, trade, loot rerolls and duplication cannot create the resource early."]
	quest.5AD13B93F716568B.quest_desc: ["Sculk Crafter is a specialized packaged-automation component in the Packaged Automation branch. It must execute an explicit recipe contract with complete inputs, a single accountable output and deterministic recovery—not act as a shortcut whose quest reward supplies black iron, awakened material or cosmic components.","Acceptance: verify contract inputs, package identity, supported recipe tier, energy or fluid cost, atomic output, backpressure, restart recovery and absence of duplicate retained contents; encode one representative recipe, submit exactly one bounded input set, reconcile package contents and final output, test missing-input, full-output and restart states, recover every retained item and confirm that rewards, duplicate packages, recursive unpacking and parallel endpoint races cannot create extra material."]
	quest.5AD13B93F716568B.title: "Sculk Crafter — Atomic Automation Acceptance"
	quest.5AD80D3242DD3F60.quest_desc: ["Insanite Block is a reactor waste, reprocessing product or high-tier material in the Extreme Reactors power branch. It must be accepted as part of a complete, instrumented multiblock whose fuel, heat, waste, coolant and output are reconciled—not as an isolated block or reward-funded power shortcut.","Acceptance: verify waste ratio per fuel batch, extraction route, reprocessing energy and reagent cost, recovered yield, residual waste, EMC and simulation restrictions and use in an authorized later-stage assembly; build or inspect the complete structure, record a cold baseline, run a bounded fuel batch, measure output and waste, test control-rod or emergency shutdown response, recover after full output or restart and confirm that rewards, duplicated fuel, free coolant and waste loops cannot create net power or gated materials."]
	quest.5AEE86EB39FD4087.quest_desc: ["Vortex Tube is a heat-transfer or temperature-control component in PneumaticCraft. Its progression value comes from pressure, heat, programmable behaviour and supporting infrastructure rather than from the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify hot and cold sides, insulation, equilibrium temperature, air cost, adjacent-machine demand and shutdown cooling; complete a representative operating cycle, record pressure, heat, air and material reserves, test shutdown or invalid input, and close loot, reward, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.5AF160257BEEF682.quest_desc: ["Glass Cable is a channel-bearing network segment in an AE2 system. The item is useful only when its power, channel, storage and routing assumptions are explicit and the network remains diagnosable under load.","Acceptance: verify channel count, controller path, colour isolation, tunnel boundaries and a visible overload diagnostic; run a representative automated job, record channel and power use, test a full or disconnected destination, and prove that loot, rewards, trades or alternate recipes cannot unlock this capability before its stage."]
	quest.5AFD4912CC8FBBB8.quest_subtitle: "Crafting ingredient"
	quest.5B0159A972A5A16C.quest_desc: ["Ice and Fire Expedition Checkpoint A16C is a Ice and Fire expedition-design checkpoint in the Ice and Fire progression branch. Its value comes from prepared exploration, first-victory evidence, controlled dragon interaction or a repeatable forge—not from receiving rare materials from the quest book.","Acceptance: verify research, equipment, cargo reserve, retreat plan, encounter proof, unique-drop storage, dragonforge safety and post-expedition recovery; document preparation and retreat criteria, complete the encounter or production cycle, reconcile unique and ordinary drops, test one failure or interrupted state and remove reward, loot-reroll, simulation, trade and duplication shortcuts."]
	quest.5B0466324A5D3718.quest_desc: ["Watch Of Flowing Time is a specialized contained-transmutation component in the contained ProjectE branch. Its use is legal only when the input was produced through the staged economy, the output is explicitly permitted and the EMC loop cannot create gated matter, unique drops or progression permissions.","Acceptance: verify legal source, EMC value or disabled status, input-output boundary, buffer, stage permission, recovery and absence of positive recursive conversion; record the EMC balance before and after a bounded cycle, test one blocked or blacklisted output, confirm storage and transfer limits, recover from a full-output or restart state and prove that quest rewards, recursive conversion, simulation, trade and duplication cannot produce net gated value."]
	quest.5B0466324A5D3718.quest_subtitle: "Best item in ProjecE"
	quest.5B1E0E3E876339E7.quest_desc: ["Supremium Helmet / Supremium Chestplate / Supremium Leggings / System is a linked agriculture system. In an expert progression pack, renewable production is permitted only after the represented resource, creature or capability has been obtained through its legitimate stage path.","Acceptance: verify component ratios, shared catalysts, legal crop tiers, output ownership and unattended completion without duplicating seeds or essences; process or harvest a representative batch with bounded automation, record yield and reserve, and prove that quest rewards, EMC, trades, loot, simulated mobs or alternate seed recipes cannot unlock or multiply this resource early."]
	quest.5B3CC3F66F2C3DE5.quest_desc: ["Seashelf is a cross-mod support item used by the Apotheosis branch in the Apotheosis progression system. It must be treated as a controlled upgrade or encounter tool whose value comes from measured build improvement, recoverable materials and explicit risk—not from a quest reward that skips the affix economy.","Acceptance: verify its exact support role, stage-appropriate availability, interaction with affixed equipment and why it assists rather than bypasses the Apotheosis system; record the before-and-after equipment state, resource cost and failure condition, test one representative combat or enchanting cycle, salvage or recover rejected results and confirm that rewards, rerolls, duplication and unrestricted boss spawning cannot bypass the intended progression."]
	quest.5B3FDF651D845DF1.quest_desc: ["Elite Mechanical Pipe is a Mekanism transport or configuration component in the first Mekanism production era. It matters only when its energy, material, chemical, transport and side-configuration contract is understood and connected to a repeatable factory.","Acceptance: verify transferred medium, pull-push direction, colour or diversion rules, throughput, network capacity, loop isolation and recovery after one segment is removed; run a representative batch, record input, output, energy and internal-buffer behaviour, test blocked output or power loss, and remove reward, EMC, loot, trade, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
