	quest.735412C77BE7A82A.quest_desc: ["Fluid Pipe / Steel Scaffolding Standard / Light Engineering / Sheetmetal Iron is a industrial logistics, fluid or bulk-storage component in the Immersive Engineering route. The objective is a measurable, serviceable industrial capability with legal inputs and recoverable failure—not a random reward for crafting one block or tool.","Acceptance: verify medium ownership, direction, redstone state, filters and priorities, throughput, finite capacity, overflow route, loop prevention and recovery after one blocked segment; build or operate a representative installation, record input, output, power or fuel and limiting section, test blocked output or loss of supply, recover safely and remove random-table, item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.735412C77BE7A82A.title: "Fluid Pipe / Steel Scaffolding Standard / Light Engineering / Sheetmetal Iron — Industrial Acceptance"
	quest.73688A75A466C834.quest_desc: ["Slice And Splice is a specialized processing machine in Ender IO. Its value comes from alloy processing, conduit topology, capacitor tier or machine configuration rather than from owning the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify recipe isolation, grinding-ball or secondary input, capacitor effect, byproducts, output blocking and restart; complete a representative unattended cycle, record energy and material reserves, test a blocked output or disconnected conduit, and close loot, reward, trade, spawner, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.73708157A391E412.quest_desc: ["Hatched from &cdetonating&r the&6 nuclear furnace&r next to this &bcreatures egg&r, this mob is &dvery powerful&r, and &acan grow&r."]
	quest.73708157A391E412.quest_subtitle: "Hatch a tremorzilla"
	quest.737570259C5A4052.quest_desc: [
		"&cThe Nuclear Furnace&r is a &bfast&r, &emultiblock structure&r created by placing &aeight Nuclear Furnace Components&r in a &lcube&r. It uses &aUranium Rods&r as fuel, with each rod capable of smelting &l60&r items. However, using the furnace produces &atoxic waste&r, which accumulates &ninside the structure&r. To manage this, players must regularly &einsert a Metal Barrel&r to purge the waste."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lIf the waste is not purged&r, the &cNuclear Furnace &rbegins to &eoverheat&r. As it &eoverheats&r, it goes through three &nvisual and physical stages&r: it starts to turn &eyellow&r, then &6shakes violently&r, and eventually &cignites fires nearby&r. While &coverheating&r does make &9smelting faster&r, it doesn't increase the number of items &aprocessed per Uranium Rod&r."
		""
		"If the &awaste&r continues to build up and is still not removed, the furnace will eventually &4explode&r in a blast similar to a &aNucleeper's&r. This explosion scatters &bUnrefined Waste&r and can also hatch any nearby &cTremorzilla Eggs&r."
	]
