	quest.76E0FA2416CF0B39.quest_desc: ["Basic Crafter is a tiered Extended Crafting package executor in the Packaged Automation branch. It must execute an explicit recipe contract with complete inputs, a single accountable output and deterministic recovery—not act as a shortcut whose quest reward supplies black iron, awakened material or cosmic components.","Acceptance: verify supported crafting tier, encoded-grid size, energy and time cost, package throughput, catalyst handling, output identity, parallel-job limit and rejection of recipes above the assigned progression stage; encode one representative recipe, submit exactly one bounded input set, reconcile package contents and final output, test missing-input, full-output and restart states, recover every retained item and confirm that rewards, duplicate packages, recursive unpacking and parallel endpoint races cannot create extra material."]
	quest.76E0FA2416CF0B39.title: "Basic Crafter — Atomic Automation Acceptance"
	quest.76E6C8B3F124B3B2.quest_desc: ["Draconium Dust is a tier-defining draconic material or core in Draconic Evolution. Its true progression value includes energy scale, modules, special abilities and infrastructure requirements rather than only the visible crafting ingredients.","Acceptance: verify material origin, previous-tier core, awakening or Chaos prerequisite, batch size and reusable progression permissions; test the complete charged or operating state, record energy and material reserves, define a recoverable failure procedure, and close loot, reward, trade, EMC, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.76F22616A4D03494.quest_desc: ["Structure Scanner is a cross-mod space-mission support component in the Stellaris space-engineering route. Its progression value depends on a documented material, life-support, propulsion, power or mission contract—not on receiving a spacecraft component from a quest reward.","Acceptance: verify which system owns production, storage, power, communication or recovery and why it supports the mission without granting an early destination or protected resource; produce or operate a representative unit, record mass or stock, energy, fuel, oxygen and recovery reserves, test one aborted or interrupted state and remove reward, trade, loot, duplication and early-planet shortcuts."]
	quest.76F51AD1E8A28949.quest_desc: ["Rabbit Foot is a cross-mod expedition support component in the Ice and Fire progression branch. Its value comes from prepared exploration, first-victory evidence, controlled dragon interaction or a repeatable forge—not from receiving rare materials from the quest book.","Acceptance: verify its role in travel, power, storage, healing or recovery and why it supports the encounter without replacing the required first victory; document preparation and retreat criteria, complete the encounter or production cycle, reconcile unique and ordinary drops, test one failure or interrupted state and remove reward, loot-reroll, simulation, trade and duplication shortcuts."]
	quest.7700E08416618198.quest_desc: [
		"Interfaces act like a small chest and fluid tank that fills itself from and empties to network storage depending on what you set it to keep a stock of in its slots. It tries to complete this in a single gametick, so it can fill itself with or empty itself from up to 9 stacks per gametick, making it a fast method of import or export if you have fast item pipes."
		""
		"Another useful trait is that while most fluid tanks can only store 1 type of fluid, interfaces can store up to 9, as well as items. They're essentially just chests/multi-fluid tanks with some extra functionality, and you can prevent that extra functionality by keeping them disconnected from any networks. Thus, they are useful in some niche cases where you want to store a small amount of a bunch of different stuff."
	]
	quest.7703240374D92007.quest_desc: ["Sag Mill is a specialized processing machine in Ender IO. Its value comes from alloy processing, conduit topology, capacitor tier or machine configuration rather than from owning the block or item alone.","Acceptance: verify recipe isolation, grinding-ball or secondary input, capacitor effect, byproducts, output blocking and restart; complete a representative unattended cycle, record energy and material reserves, test a blocked output or disconnected conduit, and close loot, reward, trade, spawner, salvage and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.773C9DA610091CFC.quest_desc: ["Push smelting to the absolute limit with extraordinary &asmelting speed&r, reconfigurable sides, &daugments&r for &csmoking&r and &2blasting&r and much more."]
	quest.773C9DA610091CFC.title: "Iron Furnace"
	quest.774AA4A99AED8B97.quest_desc: [
