	quest.774B1D4152A0B4ED.quest_desc: ["Hammer is a engineering tool, workbench or measurement reference in the Immersive Engineering route. The objective is a measurable, serviceable industrial capability with legal inputs and recoverable failure—not a random reward for crafting one block or tool.","Acceptance: verify valid targets, configuration or measurement result, durability and repair, safe use on energized machinery, stored settings, returned tools and labelled workshop storage; build or operate a representative installation, record input, output, power or fuel and limiting section, test blocked output or loss of supply, recover safely and remove random-table, item, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.77572C546A50BE0C.quest_desc: ["Shape Card Liquid is a builder or area-operation component in the RFTools ecosystem. Its capability depends on modules, cards, power, area ownership and network configuration rather than on the block alone.","Acceptance: verify shape-card bounds, chunk ownership, filter rules, energy per operation, protected blocks and output collection; run a representative automated cycle, record power and storage demand, test invalid configuration or a full destination, and close reward, loot, trade, quarry, duplication and alternate-recipe shortcuts."]
	quest.776451A1A5F3B2FB.quest_desc: ["Voltmeter is a measurement, regulation or circuit-control component in the TFMG electrical route. The lesson must establish a measured and protected power capability with reproducible conductor and component supply—not reward the player with the same wire, magnet or capacitor being requested.","Acceptance: verify measured quantity and range, probe location, expected reading, regulation rule, safe default, visible fault and calibration against a known operating state; build or operate a representative circuit, record voltage, current or capacity and the limiting component, test overload, empty generation or disconnected output, recover safely and remove material, XP and shortcut rewards."]
	quest.776C4F2AE494ADB1.quest_desc: ["2B Mega Co Processor is a cross-mod space-mission support component in the Stellaris space-engineering route. Its progression value depends on a documented material, life-support, propulsion, power or mission contract—not on receiving a spacecraft component from a quest reward.","Acceptance: verify which system owns production, storage, power, communication or recovery and why it supports the mission without granting an early destination or protected resource; produce or operate a representative unit, record mass or stock, energy, fuel, oxygen and recovery reserves, test one aborted or interrupted state and remove reward, trade, loot, duplication and early-planet shortcuts."]
