	quest.7D43016926E77150.quest_desc: ["Imperium Helmet / Imperium Chestplate / Imperium Leggings / System is a linked agriculture system. In an expert progression pack, renewable production is permitted only after the represented resource, creature or capability has been obtained through its legitimate stage path.","Acceptance: verify component ratios, shared catalysts, legal crop tiers, output ownership and unattended completion without duplicating seeds or essences; process or harvest a representative batch with bounded automation, record yield and reserve, and prove that quest rewards, EMC, trades, loot, simulated mobs or alternate seed recipes cannot unlock or multiply this resource early."]
	quest.7D4AFD1FFF1326A9.quest_desc: ["Upgrade Creative is a cross-mod convergence prerequisite for a creative permission granted only after creative convergence. Ownership is not sufficient proof: the item must have an authoritative multi-branch recipe, no alternative acquisition route and an explicit operating policy that prevents infinite output from bypassing protected resources, dimensions, encounters or progression permissions.","Acceptance: verify its source progression, assigned prior milestone, exact irreversible consumption, blacklist coverage and proof that the creative item cannot refund or recreate the prerequisite; trace the complete recipe ancestry through prior milestones, confirm EMC, simulation, loot, trade and reward blacklists, run one bounded functional test, test full-output or disconnected behavior, document safe storage and restart recovery and prove that the creative capability cannot generate unique drops, first-acquisition evidence or gated crafting permissions."]
	quest.7D557A396FB12D0A.quest_desc: ["Explorerscompass / Naturescompass is a cross-mod support item used in a utility workflow selected for a practical cross-mod workflow. The quest must explain the problem it solves, the resource or energy cost and the situations where it should not be used, rather than treating ownership as proof of mastery.","Acceptance: verify its support role, legal acquisition stage, interaction with the primary utility, replacement policy and confirmation that it does not create free resources or permissions; demonstrate one useful scenario and one misuse or failure case, measure range, capacity, speed or cost where applicable, document cleanup and recovery and confirm that the utility cannot bypass stage permissions, first encounters, protected areas or production requirements."]
	quest.7D557A396FB12D0A.title: "Explorerscompass / Naturescompass — Practical Utility Acceptance"
	quest.7D57A14810BC0CBE.quest_desc: ["Cataclysm Encounter Checkpoint 0CBE is a boss-encounter planning checkpoint in Cataclysm. Progress must come from discovering the correct structure, preparing for its mechanics and winning the legitimate encounter rather than receiving boss progress from a reward table or simulated drop source.","Acceptance: verify documented structure route, arena preparation, equipment reserve, escape and recovery plan, first-victory evidence and post-victory automation limits; document entry, arena safety, required equipment, failure recovery and first-victory evidence, then prove that Woot, neural simulation, spawners, trades, EMC, loot aliases and quest rewards cannot grant unique or capability-changing drops early."]
	quest.7DC387FEC143DEA2.quest_desc: ["Advanced Beehives / Expansion Box Oak is a cross-mod survival or workshop support component in the survival-foundations route. It should establish a safe, repeatable capability and prepare the next production step—not act as a reason to distribute ordinary materials or XP from the quest book.","Acceptance: verify which current-stage need it solves, its material ancestry, repair or refill route, limitations and why it does not grant a later technology or resource early; demonstrate a representative use, record the input, durability or reserve and output, test one loss or blocked state, keep an ordinary replacement route and remove item, XP, loot and random-reward shortcuts."]
