	quest.9D15CDB1029B4693.title: "Materials analysis workshop — prepare the route"
	quest.9D15CDB1029B4693.quest_desc: ["Before crafting the final subsystem for Field Foundations, define the legal inputs and the machine or hand-tool sequence for materials analysis workshop. The route must cover glass preparation, quartz classification, optical alignment and a repeatable comparison standard.","Prepare a labelled input buffer for at least two attempts, identify returned tools and containers, and confirm that no quest reward, trade, EMC value or later-stage machine replaces the intended work."]
	quest.18ACECAE85847DD8.title: "Materials analysis workshop — intermediate assemblies"
	quest.18ACECAE85847DD8.quest_desc: ["Produce the actual intermediate assemblies: kubejs:survey_lens. These components separate material preparation from the final mechanism and make failures diagnosable instead of hiding every cost in one 3×3 recipe.","Acceptance: produce a second set from stored ordinary materials, record the slowest input and keep one normal spare. The assemblies are consumable batch parts, not permanent permissions."]
	quest.C50C9C5AE6DCD025.title: "Materials analysis workshop — working mechanism"
	quest.C50C9C5AE6DCD025.quest_desc: ["Combine the prepared assemblies into kubejs:materials_analysis_matrix. The finished mechanism is evidence that the preceding material, tooling and control steps work together; obtaining an unrelated copy does not prove the production route.","Acceptance: inspect glass preparation, quartz classification, optical alignment and a repeatable comparison standard; perform one valid operation and one deliberately invalid or blocked operation, then return the system to a safe state without deleting rare inputs."]
	quest.4D88124E6921000A.title: "Materials analysis workshop — repeatable production"
	quest.4D88124E6921000A.quest_desc: ["Turn materials analysis workshop into a repeatable part of Field Foundations. Feed inputs from labelled storage, route every output and byproduct, and remove the need to rearrange inventories between normal cycles.","Run a representative unattended batch, record input rate, output rate and reserve, and prove that empty input or full output stops only this branch rather than deadlocking the whole stage."]
	quest.54C9C94635B40D61.title: "Regulated wiring bench — prepare the route"
	quest.54C9C94635B40D61.quest_desc: ["Before crafting the final subsystem for Field Foundations, define the legal inputs and the machine or hand-tool sequence for regulated wiring bench. The route must cover insulation, polarity, redstone control, motor demand and safe isolation of the first powered workbench.","Prepare a labelled input buffer for at least two attempts, identify returned tools and containers, and confirm that no quest reward, trade, EMC value or later-stage machine replaces the intended work."]
	quest.D551873FC45CBAE4.title: "Regulated wiring bench — intermediate assemblies"
	quest.D551873FC45CBAE4.quest_desc: ["Produce the actual intermediate assemblies: kubejs:insulated_wiring_bundle, kubejs:manual_control_board. These components separate material preparation from the final mechanism and make failures diagnosable instead of hiding every cost in one 3×3 recipe.","Acceptance: produce a second set from stored ordinary materials, record the slowest input and keep one normal spare. The assemblies are consumable batch parts, not permanent permissions."]
	quest.EDF6724885D2BFA1.title: "Regulated wiring bench — working mechanism"
	quest.EDF6724885D2BFA1.quest_desc: ["Combine the prepared assemblies into kubejs:power_regulation_unit. The finished mechanism is evidence that the preceding material, tooling and control steps work together; obtaining an unrelated copy does not prove the production route.","Acceptance: inspect insulation, polarity, redstone control, motor demand and safe isolation of the first powered workbench; perform one valid operation and one deliberately invalid or blocked operation, then return the system to a safe state without deleting rare inputs."]
	quest.7426D4D3DCACEEB4.title: "Regulated wiring bench — repeatable production"
	quest.7426D4D3DCACEEB4.quest_desc: ["Turn regulated wiring bench into a repeatable part of Field Foundations. Feed inputs from labelled storage, route every output and byproduct, and remove the need to rearrange inventories between normal cycles.","Run a representative unattended batch, record input rate, output rate and reserve, and prove that empty input or full output stops only this branch rather than deadlocking the whole stage."]
	quest.78AEFCF74E5FC39B.title: "Field tooling and repair — prepare the route"
	quest.78AEFCF74E5FC39B.quest_desc: ["Before crafting the final subsystem for Field Foundations, define the legal inputs and the machine or hand-tool sequence for field tooling and repair. The route must cover reusable tools, protected spares, repair access and a compact kit layout that survives an early-base failure.","Prepare a labelled input buffer for at least two attempts, identify returned tools and containers, and confirm that no quest reward, trade, EMC value or later-stage machine replaces the intended work."]
	quest.C6BF4F4DA16E54CA.title: "Field tooling and repair — intermediate assemblies"
	quest.C6BF4F4DA16E54CA.quest_desc: ["Produce the actual intermediate assemblies: kubejs:field_tool_frame. These components separate material preparation from the final mechanism and make failures diagnosable instead of hiding every cost in one 3×3 recipe.","Acceptance: produce a second set from stored ordinary materials, record the slowest input and keep one normal spare. The assemblies are consumable batch parts, not permanent permissions."]
	quest.52055CAFDDCA60B3.title: "Field tooling and repair — working mechanism"
	quest.52055CAFDDCA60B3.quest_desc: ["Combine the prepared assemblies into the verified subsystem. The finished mechanism is evidence that the preceding material, tooling and control steps work together; obtaining an unrelated copy does not prove the production route.","Acceptance: inspect reusable tools, protected spares, repair access and a compact kit layout that survives an early-base failure; perform one valid operation and one deliberately invalid or blocked operation, then return the system to a safe state without deleting rare inputs."]
	quest.7A016D625006D943.title: "Field tooling and repair — repeatable production"
	quest.7A016D625006D943.quest_desc: ["Turn field tooling and repair into a repeatable part of Field Foundations. Feed inputs from labelled storage, route every output and byproduct, and remove the need to rearrange inventories between normal cycles.","Run a representative unattended batch, record input rate, output rate and reserve, and prove that empty input or full output stops only this branch rather than deadlocking the whole stage."]
	quest.6EC9CB6DA2DD5FD5.title: "Optimization — Measure the baseline"
	quest.6EC9CB6DA2DD5FD5.quest_desc: ["Measure one normal cycle of Stage 1 before changing the design. Record manual batch time, tool travel, protected storage, idle furnaces and recovery after losing one workstation; a faster machine is irrelevant when another branch is already limiting the batch.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.C166987B70CFE0D2.title: "Optimization — Find the real bottleneck"
	quest.C166987B70CFE0D2.quest_desc: ["Increase demand gradually and identify the first queue, empty input or overloaded network. Change only the limiting section and compare the result with the recorded baseline.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.70E00936F0ED109B.title: "Optimization — Right-size buffers"
	quest.70E00936F0ED109B.quest_desc: ["Size input, intermediate and output buffers from measured rates. Keep enough reserve for recovery, but avoid inventories so large that a fault remains hidden for hours.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.AF977F4861754554.title: "Optimization — Control idle cost"
	quest.AF977F4861754554.quest_desc: ["Stop avoidable power, fuel, rotation, pressure or entity work when demand is absent. The shutdown must not lose recipe state, void inputs or require rebuilding the line.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.3ECD04191B5648C8.title: "Optimization — Recover after reload"
	quest.3ECD04191B5648C8.quest_desc: ["Reload the relevant chunks or simulate a clean restart. Verify filters, directions, ownership and machine state, then document the shortest safe recovery procedure.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.9AE90D0A4712970D.title: "Stage 1 integration build"
	quest.9AE90D0A4712970D.quest_desc: ["Combine the completed production branches and the optimization branch into the stage capability kubejs:field_engineering_kit. Preserve clear buffers between subsystems so a failure has one visible owner.","Produce the integration item through the authoritative recipe, verify every prerequisite branch remains reproducible, and reject any alternate acquisition that skips an intermediate assembly or a declared earlier-stage standard."]
	quest.08131E6EFFEDFA84.title: "Stage 1 recovery rehearsal"
	quest.08131E6EFFEDFA84.quest_desc: ["Before professional stage certification, rehearse recovery from one failed branch: isolate it, preserve healthy buffers, replace ordinary consumables and restart in the documented order.","Keep the integration item as proof, restore a production-ready spare batch and confirm that the following certification quests can be completed without administrator commands, creative items or random rewards."]
	quest.4493AF5EDDAC0D3C.title: "Structural standard line — prepare the route"
	quest.4493AF5EDDAC0D3C.quest_desc: ["Before crafting the final subsystem for Steam and Metallurgy, define the legal inputs and the machine or hand-tool sequence for structural standard line. The route must cover repeatable bracing, dimensional consistency, returned field tooling and a common mounting standard for later machines.","Prepare a labelled input buffer for at least two attempts, identify returned tools and containers, and confirm that no quest reward, trade, EMC value or later-stage machine replaces the intended work."]
