	quest.C1535499970884EF.quest_desc: ["Increase demand gradually and identify the first queue, empty input or overloaded network. Change only the limiting section and compare the result with the recorded baseline.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.0DE55560B6940704.title: "Optimization — Right-size buffers"
	quest.0DE55560B6940704.quest_desc: ["Size input, intermediate and output buffers from measured rates. Keep enough reserve for recovery, but avoid inventories so large that a fault remains hidden for hours.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.EE6E96552974B7A2.title: "Optimization — Control idle cost"
	quest.EE6E96552974B7A2.quest_desc: ["Stop avoidable power, fuel, rotation, pressure or entity work when demand is absent. The shutdown must not lose recipe state, void inputs or require rebuilding the line.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.92E0732DB1CFBBF2.title: "Optimization — Recover after reload"
	quest.92E0732DB1CFBBF2.quest_desc: ["Reload the relevant chunks or simulate a clean restart. Verify filters, directions, ownership and machine state, then document the shortest safe recovery procedure.","Acceptance requires a before/after observation and a concrete design change; checking the box without measuring or modifying the system is not completion."]
	quest.0FFF80D98E7B7E2F.title: "Stage 9 integration build"
	quest.0FFF80D98E7B7E2F.quest_desc: ["Combine the completed production branches and the optimization branch into the stage capability kubejs:bioindustrial_matrix. Preserve clear buffers between subsystems so a failure has one visible owner.","Produce the integration item through the authoritative recipe, verify every prerequisite branch remains reproducible, and reject any alternate acquisition that skips an intermediate assembly or a declared earlier-stage standard."]
	quest.70560620AB320004.title: "Stage 9 recovery rehearsal"
	quest.70560620AB320004.quest_desc: ["Before professional stage certification, rehearse recovery from one failed branch: isolate it, preserve healthy buffers, replace ordinary consumables and restart in the documented order.","Keep the integration item as proof, restore a production-ready spare batch and confirm that the following certification quests can be completed without administrator commands, creative items or random rewards."]
	quest.2D09C86E9843367E.title: "Controller-scale channel network — prepare the route"
	quest.2D09C86E9843367E.quest_desc: ["Before crafting the final subsystem for Applied Logistics, define the legal inputs and the machine or hand-tool sequence for controller-scale channel network. The route must cover controller shape, power reserve, channel topology, dense-cable handoff and isolation of a saturated network face.","Prepare a labelled input buffer for at least two attempts, identify returned tools and containers, and confirm that no quest reward, trade, EMC value or later-stage machine replaces the intended work."]
	quest.5279C8A60C4EE40D.title: "Controller-scale channel network — intermediate assemblies"
	quest.5279C8A60C4EE40D.quest_desc: ["Produce the actual intermediate assemblies: kubejs:controller_channel_frame. These components separate material preparation from the final mechanism and make failures diagnosable instead of hiding every cost in one 3×3 recipe.","Acceptance: produce a second set from stored ordinary materials, record the slowest input and keep one normal spare. The assemblies are consumable batch parts, not permanent permissions."]
	quest.5E3E7614A3A626EC.title: "Controller-scale channel network — working mechanism"
	quest.5E3E7614A3A626EC.quest_desc: ["Combine the prepared assemblies into ae2:controller. The finished mechanism is evidence that the preceding material, tooling and control steps work together; obtaining an unrelated copy does not prove the production route.","Acceptance: inspect controller shape, power reserve, channel topology, dense-cable handoff and isolation of a saturated network face; perform one valid operation and one deliberately invalid or blocked operation, then return the system to a safe state without deleting rare inputs."]
	quest.279D87C0EE38A9D6.title: "Controller-scale channel network — repeatable production"
	quest.279D87C0EE38A9D6.quest_desc: ["Turn controller-scale channel network into a repeatable part of Applied Logistics. Feed inputs from labelled storage, route every output and byproduct, and remove the need to rearrange inventories between normal cycles.","Run a representative unattended batch, record input rate, output rate and reserve, and prove that empty input or full output stops only this branch rather than deadlocking the whole stage."]
